    "https://jobs.tufts.edu/jobs/23404?lang=en-us": {
      "title": "Catering Events Manager in Medford, Massachusetts",
      "description": "Catering Events Manager in Medford, Massachusetts | Tufts University Skip to Main Content toggle menu CLOSE About Benefits Opportunities DEI Community Open Positions Back Catering Events Manager JOB_DESCRIPTION.SHARE.HTML CAROUSEL_PARAGRAPH JOB_DESCRIPTION.SHARE.HTML Medford, Massachusetts On-Site Dining 23404 mail_outline Get future jobs matching this search Login or Register Job Description Overview Tufts Dining is a self-operated food service provider managing a comprehensive collegiate food service program on the Tufts University Medford/Somerville and Boston/Fenway (SMFA) campuses, delivering high quality, contemporary, and innovative food, and hospitality services to meet the various needs of students, faculty, staff, administrators and visitors in a fiscally responsible manner. Our team operates a progressive resident dining program as well as innovative retail services, and a distinctive university catering program serving a campus community comprised of 6500 undergraduates, 2100 graduate students, and 2300 staff, faculty and administrators. Please review the Application Instructions under \"What We're Looking For\" for specific guidance on submitting your cover letter. What You'll Do The Tufts Catering Event Manager position exists to execute all catering services performed by Tufts Catering. Duties include but are not limited to managing catered events in person, staff management and delivering exceptional customer catering service. This integral management for Tufts Catering will train staff to industry standards, fully understand the hospitality industry at the highest level and will strive to make our unit the preferred Catering Partner to the University Community. Foodservice management and catering skills to include knowledge of all standard and VIP catering services and techniques Continue to solidify Tufts Catering goal to be the preferred catering partner on campus. Support and pursue all of Tufts Dining Department wide goals Ability to plan and organize assigned staff both verbally and in writing with clear directions Manage Staff in adherence of Collective Bargaining Contract Train staff to achieve exceptional Catering service techniques Preparing and posting weekly Catering Staff schedules as business dictates Execute Units plan to be more revenue minded by thorough planning and scheduling Guarantee stellar customer service to ensure repeat business What We're Looking For Basic Requirements: Knowledge and experience typically acquired by: Knowledge and experience typically acquired through the completion of a High School/equivalent. Experience in planning and executing events for a high-volume off-site caterer for a university, hotel, or banquet facility with multiple venues 2+ years of scheduling and supervising full-service catering staff Valid Massachusetts Driver's License in good standing with no restrictions Fine dining and modern catering concept experience such as interactive food stations, themed receptions, and VIP events Experience with responsible alcohol service and knowledge of bar, wine, and cocktail service Has experience managing multiple events at one time Culinary experience in high-end catering service or restaurants Preferred Qualifications: Associate's Degree or above, preferably in Hospitality, Management, or Business Application Instructions: In addition to your resume, please submit a brief cover letter describing your experience and interest in the Catering Events Manager role. Candidates are encouraged to highlight relevant experience in catering operations, including planning, coordinating, and executing high-volume events, VIP functions, receptions, and other hospitality services. We also welcome examples of team leadership, staff development, and experience working in a unionized environment. Additionally, feel free to share what draws you to Tufts Dining and how your professional goals align with this opportunity. We encourage concise, focused responses rather than general statements of interest. Pay Range Minimum $55,600.00, Midpoint $69,500.00, Maximum $83,400.00 Salary is based on related experience, expertise, and internal equity; generally, new hires can expect pay between the minimum and midpoint of the range. Apply Refer JOB_DESCRIPTION.SHARE.HTML CAROUSEL_PARAGRAPH JOB_DESCRIPTION.SHARE.HTML An employee in this position must complete all appropriate background checks at the time of hire, promotion, or transfer. Tufts University is an equal opportunity employer. Tufts Non-Discrimination Statement Tufts Annual Security Report On Campus Safety Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Accessibility Privacy © Tufts University 2026 Cookies are used on this site to assist in continually improving the candidate experience and all the interaction data we store of our visitors is anonymous. Learn more about your rights on our Privacy Policy page. Okay x"
