    "https://jobs.tufts.edu/jobs/23656?lang=en-us": {
      "title": "Pre-Award Research Administrator II in Boston, Massachusetts",
      "description": "Pre-Award Research Administrator II in Boston, Massachusetts | Tufts University Skip to Main Content toggle menu CLOSE About Benefits Opportunities DEI Community Open Positions Back Pre-Award Research Administrator II JOB_DESCRIPTION.SHARE.HTML CAROUSEL_PARAGRAPH JOB_DESCRIPTION.SHARE.HTML Boston, Massachusetts Remote Research Administration 23656 mail_outline Get future jobs matching this search Login or Register Job Description Overview The Office of University Research and Innovation (OURI) strives to provide high-quality services to faculty and staff and to increase the funding available to support research and scholarship, while protecting the university's interests and ensuring compliance with all relevant laws and regulations. The office works in collaboration with university leadership, faculty, staff, and students to advance strategic initiatives that strengthen Tufts' research enterprise and ensure institutional obligations are met. OURI is responsible for pre-award administration of grants and contracts and supports investigators in developing proposals and funding strategies. The office partners with other administrative units to support an environment that advances research, scholarship, innovation, and entrepreneurship across the university. The Pre-Award Research Administrator II plays a key role in advancing Tufts' research mission by administering a portfolio of broad and moderately complex sponsored programs. This position is eligible for a fully remote work arrangement. What You'll Do As a member of OURI, the Pre-Award Research Administrator II works closely with faculty, departmental research administrators, and sponsors to support the successful development, submission, and administration of externally funded research projects. This role serves as a trusted resource on sponsor requirements, institutional policies, and research administration best practices. Responsibilities include: Manage a portfolio of approximately 120 sponsored research proposals annually. Review, prepare, and process sponsored research proposals to ensure compliance with sponsor requirements and university policies, including budget review and verification of allowable costs Partner with principal investigators and departmental research administrators throughout the proposal development and submission process. Prepare subcontract agreements and amendments using established institutional templates and procedures. Negotiate agreements with standard terms and conditions prior to authorized official review and signature. Provide non-financial post-award support, including budget reallocations, no-cost extensions, contract amendments, and interpretation of award terms and conditions. Serve as a trusted resource to principal investigators and departmental research administrators by providing guidance on sponsor requirements, university policies, and research administration best practices. Maintain and develop expertise in research administration through ongoing monitoring of sponsor requirements, policies, and funding updates. Participate in special projects and respond to reporting and information requests as needed. Assist in training and onboarding junior and temporary staff. Attend meetings and collaborate with colleagues across the university to support research administration activities. What We're Looking For Application Instructions: To apply, please submit the following materials: 1.) Resume 2.) Cover Letter. Your cover letter should briefly describe your interest in this role, your motivation for supporting research at Tufts, and the key skills or experiences that make you a strong fit for a Pre‑Award Research Administrator II position. Basic Requirements: Knowledge and experience typically acquired by: Knowledge and skills typically acquired through a Bachelor’s degree or equivalent experience. 3+ years of research administration experience, including proposal review and sponsored project support. Knowledge of major funding agencies, sponsor requirements, and electronic research administration systems (e.g., Grants.gov, NIH eRA Commons, NSF FastLane/Research.gov, ProposalCentral), or the ability to learn new systems quickly. Understanding of federal regulations governing sponsored research and related areas of compliance. Proficiency in Microsoft Office (Outlook, Word, Excel, PowerPoint). Strong attention to detail, judgment, analytical skills, and ability to manage multiple concurrent deadlines. Strong communication and customer‑service skills. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a fast‑paced, deadline‑driven environment. Preferred Qualifications: Professional certification such as Certified Research Administrator (CRA), Certified Pre‑Award Research Administrator (CPRA), or Certified Financial Research Administrator (CFRA). Pay Range Minimum $67,200.00, Midpoint $83,900.00, Maximum $100,700.00 Salary is based on related experience, expertise, and internal equity; generally, new hires can expect pay between the minimum and midpoint of the range. Apply Refer JOB_DESCRIPTION.SHARE.HTML CAROUSEL_PARAGRAPH JOB_DESCRIPTION.SHARE.HTML An employee in this position must complete all appropriate background checks at the time of hire, promotion, or transfer. Tufts University is an equal opportunity employer. Tufts Non-Discrimination Statement Tufts Annual Security Report On Campus Safety Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Accessibility Privacy © Tufts University 2026 Cookies are used on this site to assist in continually improving the candidate experience and all the interaction data we store of our visitors is anonymous. Learn more about your rights on our Privacy Policy page. Okay x"
    },
